# Nothing that is not source enters the build context.
#
# This matters more than build speed: the context is what a layer can capture,
# and a credential or a recorded response that reaches a layer stays in the
# image. The repository already excludes those from Git; this excludes them
# from the image even on a working copy where they are present.

# Credentials and local configuration, in every form.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx

# Version control and local tooling.
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github
node_modules
coverage
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# The one-shot live-call probe and its guards. Excluded from the repository
# too: it contacts a real endpoint and consumes quota. An image that could run
# it would turn a container start into a billable call.
runtime/live-once.mjs
runtime/.live-api-attempted
runtime/tests/live-once.test.mjs

# Recorded API responses: execution data, never image content.
runtime/tests/fixtures/captured/
**/fixtures/captured/
*.captured.json
observation.json
report_*.json

# Internal reports and the container artefacts themselves.
runtime/REFERENCE_AND_LOOPBACK_REPORT.md
runtime/FINALISATION_REPORT.md
runtime/PUBLICATION_READINESS_REPORT.md
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
compose.yaml
